# near_repeated_half_vs_zstd3: bottom half a near repeat of the top: 980 cells differ, clustered in 89 of the 512 8x8s (169 of the 2048 4x4s); blocky texture, runs about 4 long; zstd matches the rows 4 KiB back past the differences, gct's copies need exact tiles, so each difference breaks the copy of every tile around it
